# The Expression hexagon — a grammar chapter, held in memory.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE. This used to name Memory once per aggregate :
#
#   Expression::Operator.persisted_by("Memory")
#   Expression::Normalisation.persisted_by("Memory")
#   …
#
# which is four lines saying "no decision", and one more every time the chapter
# grows an aggregate — a line whose absence, once an unbound aggregate became an
# error, was a boot failure rather than the obvious default.
#
# Memory is what an aggregate gets when nobody wires it. A grammar chapter is a
# conception : it is reasoned about far more often than it is stored, so it
# claims no database, and now says so by saying nothing. Wiring is override, not
# substrate — the file stays because the hexagon is still the place a decision
# WOULD go, and there is simply no decision to record.
Hecks.hecksagon "Expression" do
end
